dot {A}^{T}\\ne I,$ our matrix is **not** orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287788 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3145a3cc-a8fa-5e22-9409-4c06adc4e92d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285233} {:answer/id #uuid "5171921f-5b71-50ae-8b05-c9689f2a44a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285536} {:answer/id #uuid "8477874d-308e-51fd-aac0-c1299491c71e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286006} {:answer/id #uuid "abace7ca-ea67-5b94-8452-b153ad1c9de2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286357} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e0bac0-87ad-598f-a0f8-584b58cdd803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2e0bac0-87ad-598f-a0f8-584b58cdd803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286855} :answer-field/id #uuid "75ac9360-e05a-56fb-93b2-7d5feaa1faad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287397}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "110cd0b0-c05f-5fa3-a734-2910b10ec096" :question/math-academy-id "q-182009" :question/problem "For the sets $A={k,m},$ $B={-1,3,5},$ and $C=A\\times B,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(-1,k)\\in C$\n- $(k,m)\\in C$\n- $(m,3)\\in C$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $A\\times B$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/c6/c660ff6d042bdf228387e5ad55651f02b136f738a2e4fa99c3ef3b3faef3e3c5.png)\n\nHence, the set $C=A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nC={(k,-1),(k,3),(k,5),(m,-1),(m,3),(m,5)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15b36e5f-e8a8-5ea9-946e-c4816a26e689" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284982} {:answer/id #uuid "2d977033-ec3f-53cc-a677-5319105de312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285193} {:answer/id #uuid "3418f9d4-3146-507c-b45f-2efcc9ed4974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285266} {:answer/id #uuid "65a4153e-cfe4-5447-acfc-d029e30792b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285710} {:answer/id #uuid "88dd20ce-84ae-5cec-b98c-0addd3860395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d977033-ec3f-53cc-a677-5319105de312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285193} :answer-field/id #uuid "80e9eb6a-880b-5e87-86c2-04da9fdfec7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2efc8f2-dfe5-5b29-94dc-09dde2c27a4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-182015" :question/problem "For the sets $X=\\{5,10\\},$ $Y=\\{r,s,t\\},$ and $Z=X\\times Y,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\nI. $(5,r)\\in Z$\n\nII. $(r,t)\\in Z$\n\nIII. $(10,s)\\in Z$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $X\\times Y$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Y.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $X\\times Y$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/1e/1eb13d93fbefc4c7285edef537a9fb3e21339f7a3b37a179eeb150db8d726c1b.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(5,r),(5,s),(5,t),(10,r),(10,s),(10,t)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287793 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ba40535-7a9b-5dd6-81a0-8660440ecd3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284880} {:answer/id #uuid "39a54562-da76-5262-94d8-dae03a4de002" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285330} {:answer/id #uuid "aedcddb9-24f3-5bcd-9e4e-186ed907f4a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286381} {:answer/id #uuid "b70faa1d-b0bd-5a05-be76-576658ffc59d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286458} {:answer/id #uuid "c95ea54e-b8a5-5e00-8424-a086b6273b63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c95ea54e-b8a5-5e00-8424-a086b6273b63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286624} :answer-field/id #uuid "5203f15a-1200-56ea-98bd-cfd61c7ca2ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "55b1acd6-5df7-5bc0-a3b3-0f00f1d5d19b" :question/math-academy-id "q-182018" :question/problem "For the sets $X={f,g,h}$ and $Z=X\\times X,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(f,g)\\in Z$\n- $(f,g,h)\\in Z$\n- $(h,h)\\in Z$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $X\\times X$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $X.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for ${X}^{2}=X\\times X$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/17/1718bd6f3f2eaa8dd8fe581b0d938b3b5f1928d5e56a11a324f145e7a481fabe.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times X$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(f,f),(f,g),(f,h),(g,f),(g,g),(g,h),(h,f),(h,g),(h,h)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}]}
